# Act Provider

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

## Authentication

Create an API key in the Act console under Settings → API keys, then give the provider its client ID and secret. Keep the secret out of the configuration by setting `ACT_CLIENT_SECRET`.

The provider learns the tenant from the key's token and asks the Act STS at `auth.act.security` which regional public API serves it, so you never set a tenant ID or an API URL. Setting `tenant_id` or `region` only adds a check that the key belongs to the tenant, or the tenant lives in the region, you expect.

| Setting | Environment variable | Required |
|---|---|---|
| `client_id` | `ACT_CLIENT_ID` | yes |
| `client_secret` | `ACT_CLIENT_SECRET` | yes |
| `tenant_id` | `ACT_TENANT_ID` | no |
| `region` | `ACT_REGION` | no |

## Retries

The provider retries a request up to 4 times when the Act STS or API answers `429`, `502`, `503` or `504`, when the API marks an error as retryable, or when the connection fails. It waits with exponential backoff and honours `Retry-After` up to 30 seconds. Certificate errors and requests the server rejected are never retried.

When the API answers `401`, the provider gets a new token once and repeats the request.

